  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Mother
    dialogueText: Doctor, please, you have to help! My son, Leo, he can't breathe
      properly! He's coughing so much and his chest is making a whistling sound.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Doctor
    dialogueText: Stay calm, ma'am, we're here to help him. I'm going to assess him
      right away. Has this ever happened before?
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Mother
    dialogueText: Yes, he was diagnosed with asthma last year, but it's never been
      this bad. We used his rescue inhaler at home but it didn't seem to help much.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Doctor
    dialogueText: (To the child) Hey there, champ. My name is Dr. [Your Name]. I'm
      going to help you breathe much easier, okay? Can you take a big breath for
      me?
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Child
    dialogueText: (Wheezing, speaks with difficulty) ...I can't... it hurts...
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Doctor
    dialogueText: Okay, I can hear the wheezing clearly and his oxygen saturation
      is a bit low. We need to act fast. We're starting a nebulizer treatment with
      Albuterol immediately.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Mother
    dialogueText: A nebulizer? Is that the machine with the mist? Will it work?
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Doctor
    dialogueText: Yes, exactly. The medicated mist will go deep into his lungs to
      open up his airways. It's the most effective first-line treatment for a severe
      asthma attack.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 1
    characterName: 
    dialogueText: 
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 1790930194}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Doctor
    dialogueText: Great, the treatment has started. This will help relax the muscles
      in his airways, making it much easier for him to breathe. We'll monitor his
      response closely.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Mother
    dialogueText: Oh, thank you, doctor. Is he going to be okay? I was so scared.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Doctor
    dialogueText: He's responding well to the treatment. Asthma attacks can be frightening,
      but we're managing it. The most important thing is what we do after this to
      prevent it from happening again.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Doctor
    dialogueText: We'll need to review his Asthma Action Plan. It seems his current
      plan isn't enough to control his symptoms.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Mother
    dialogueText: His action plan? The school nurse mentioned that. I'm not sure
      I fully understand it.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Doctor
    dialogueText: It's a simple guide that tells us what to do every day, and what
      to do when his symptoms get worse. We'll create a new, clearer one for you
      before you leave.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Child
    dialogueText: (Voice is clearer, less strained) ...The mist feels cold... I can
      breathe a little better.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Doctor
    dialogueText: That's excellent news, Leo! You're doing a great job. We're going
      to check your breathing with a stethoscope again now.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Doctor
    dialogueText: The wheezing is much quieter now, and his oxygen levels are back
      to normal. That's a fantastic response to the first treatment.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Mother
    dialogueText: So, what happens now? Can we go home?
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Doctor
    dialogueText: We'll keep him for observation for a little while longer to ensure
      he remains stable. We may give one more treatment before discharge and provide
      a short course of oral steroids.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Doctor
    dialogueText: Remember, consistent use of his daily controller inhaler is key
      to preventing these attacks. The rescue inhaler is for emergencies, not for
      daily use.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Mother
    dialogueText: I understand now. Thank you so much, Doctor. You've been a great
      help.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  - eventType: 0
    characterName: Mother
    dialogueText: I understand now. Thank you so much, Doctor. You've been a great
      help.
    dialogueAudio: {fileID: 0}
    taskObject: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueUIManager: {fileID: 196443544}
